l Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a wetter season with more rainy days, and this year's shift is a noticeable tilt. Relative humidity has fallen by about 0.3 points per decade, roughly 3 points since 1951; because warmer air holds more moisture, this does not necessarily mean the air is drier. El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a more humid Mar–May, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. For Mar–May 2027, a warmer-than-normal season has about even odds (about 50%), about 0.3 °C above the 1991–2020 average, mostly because of the long-term warming trend rather than El Niño; a more humid season than normal is more likely than not (about 60%). The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":22.8252,"trend_per_decade":0.0882,"trend_p":0.041,"trend_total_since_1951":0.6611,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.06,"enso_p":0.5459,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","survives_fdr":false,"fraction_explained":0.0051,"intrinsic_sd":0.7867,"effect_this_season":0.1059,"effect_ratio":0.1346,"size":"Negligible","size_typical_el_nino":"Negligible","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":null,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.3106,"forecast_mean":23.1358,"forecast_sd":0.8394,"p_below":0.2482,"p_near":0.2472,"p_above":0.5046,"forecast_words":"About even odds (50%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":false,"enso_effect_shrunk_per_degC":0.0419,"shrink_factor":0.6974,"effect_this_season_raw":0.1519,"trend_part_2027":0.2046,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":12.0138,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.0514,"trend_p":0.6203,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.2054,"enso_p":0.3727,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shif